       "text": "I entered the order as you confirmed it: sertraline 1000 mg by mouth once daily (Order ID: ORD-0001).\n\nI added a note to the order. It says the dose exceeds the maximum labeled adult dose of 200 mg/day. It also says you confirmed the dose is intentional and will document your rationale in the chart. It asks pharmacy to verify the order, so expect a call from them about it.\n\nAt this dose the patient needs close monitoring for serotonin toxicity, which can show up as agitation, tremor, hyperthermia, tachycardia, or clonus. An ECG for QTc and monitoring for seizures and hyponatremia are also reasonable. Please also check for other serotonergic or QT-prolonging drugs on the patient's medication list."
